1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,264
Alright, welcome back to Car Detailing
Podcast. I'm Alex.

2
00:00:04,614 --> 00:00:09,606
And I'm Sam. Today we're talking rims.
Fresh paint, fresh look.

3
00:00:09,956 --> 00:00:14,852
Car Rim Painting at Desert Diamond, Dubai.
Al Quoz Industrial Area 3.

4
00:00:15,202 --> 00:00:22,114
And we've got a guest who just did it.
British expat, dry humour, bought a car

5
00:00:22,463 --> 00:00:25,079
Welcome to the show. How's Dubai treating
you?

6
00:00:25,429 --> 00:00:31,837
Hot. Expensive. Full of roundabouts I
still don't understand.

7
00:00:32,187 --> 00:00:36,387
Sounds about right. So — new car. What did
you get?

8
00:00:36,737 --> 00:00:44,081
A used German sedan. Lovely engine. Wheels
looked like they'd survived a war.

9
00:00:44,431 --> 00:00:45,295
Curb rash?

10
00:00:45,645 --> 00:00:52,629
Curb rash, corrosion, mystery stains.
Previous owner clearly parked by braille.

11
00:00:52,979 --> 00:00:57,779
Ouch. So you booked rim painting. How did
you find Desert Diamond?

12
00:00:58,129 --> 00:01:08,449
Googled 'rim painting Dubai'. Their site
came up. car-care.center. Clean layout.

13
00:01:08,798 --> 00:01:09,398
Easy?

14
00:01:09,748 --> 00:01:17,332
Stupidly easy. Picked a slot. Got
confirmation. No back-and-forth.

15
00:01:17,682 --> 00:01:23,850
Nice. And the studio — Al Quoz, 22nd
Street. What was your first impression?

16
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:32,960
Pulled up. Thought I'd wandered into a
surgery. Spotless. Organised. No clutter.

17
00:01:33,310 --> 00:01:34,486
They run a tight ship.

18
00:01:34,836 --> 00:01:42,180
European-trained specialists, they said.
Felt like it. No one scratching their

19
00:01:42,530 --> 00:01:46,610
Walk us through the process. What happened
when you handed over the keys?

20
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:53,608
They inspected each wheel. Took photos.
Showed me the damage up close.

21
00:01:53,957 --> 00:01:54,773
On a screen?

22
00:01:55,123 --> 00:02:04,075
On a tablet. Zoomed in. 'See this pitting?
This clear coat failure?' Very thorough.

23
00:02:04,425 --> 00:02:05,145
And then?

24
00:02:05,495 --> 00:02:16,631
Wheels off. Chemical strip. Sandblasting.
Primer. Base coat. Clear coat. Oven bake.

25
00:02:16,981 --> 00:02:17,725
Oven bake?

26
00:02:18,075 --> 00:02:24,675
Big curing oven. Proper finish. Not a
rattle can in a car park.

27
00:02:25,025 --> 00:02:26,705
How long were you without the car?

28
00:02:27,055 --> 00:02:33,391
Dropped it at nine. Picked it up late
afternoon. They texted when ready.

29
00:02:33,740 --> 00:02:34,700
That's a full day.

30
00:02:35,050 --> 00:02:42,274
Worth it. Came back, wheels looked
factory. Better than factory, honestly.

31
00:02:42,624 --> 00:02:43,536
Colour match?

32
00:02:43,886 --> 00:02:50,366
OEM silver. Couldn't tell they'd been
touched. Even the inner barrels.

33
00:02:50,716 --> 00:02:51,988
They do the barrels too?

34
00:02:52,338 --> 00:02:58,938
Full wheel. Inside and out. Said it
prevents corrosion creeping back.

35
00:02:59,288 --> 00:03:03,560
Smart. And the price — 500 AED for the
set?

36
00:03:03,910 --> 00:03:12,502
500 AED. All four. No hidden extras. Paid
what the site said.

37
00:03:12,851 --> 00:03:13,739
No upsell?

38
00:03:14,089 --> 00:03:22,297
They mentioned ceramic coating for wheels.
Optional. I passed. Maybe next time.

39
00:03:22,647 --> 00:03:24,375
How did it feel driving away?

40
00:03:24,725 --> 00:03:31,685
Weird. Kept glancing at the side mirrors
just to see the wheels. Felt new.

41
00:03:32,035 --> 00:03:32,995
That's the feeling.

42
00:03:33,345 --> 00:03:41,505
Drove past a reflective building. Slowed
down. Admired them. Not even ashamed.

43
00:03:41,855 --> 00:03:45,407
Best kind of vanity. Any aftercare advice
from them?

44
00:03:45,757 --> 00:03:54,709
Gentle wash for a week. No harsh
chemicals. pH-neutral shampoo. Soft brush.

45
00:03:55,058 --> 00:03:57,506
Makes sense. So — worth it?

46
00:03:57,856 --> 00:04:06,064
Every dirham. Car looks complete now.
Wheels match the paint. Whole thing lifts.

47
00:04:06,414 --> 00:04:09,150
Love that. Thanks for sharing the story.

48
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:12,212
Right. Let's bring in Omar for a quick
tip.

49
00:04:12,562 --> 00:04:17,962
Hey guys. Question came in: how often
should I wash my car in the UAE climate?

50
00:04:18,312 --> 00:04:21,408
Good one. Dust, sand, humidity.

51
00:04:21,758 --> 00:04:29,966
Weekly at minimum. Desert Diamond's car
wash starts at 85 AED. pH-neutral, safe on

52
00:04:30,316 --> 00:04:33,988
Weekly. Noted. And don't use dish soap.

53
00:04:34,337 --> 00:04:41,057
Never. Strips protection. Use proper
shampoo. Two-bucket method if you DIY.

54
00:04:41,407 --> 00:04:43,855
Solid tip. Thanks, Omar.

55
00:04:44,205 --> 00:04:45,141
Anytime.

56
00:04:45,491 --> 00:04:49,283
Okay — Myth Busting time. One myth,
busted.

57
00:04:49,633 --> 00:04:53,713
Myth: 'Rim painting is just cosmetic. It
doesn't protect anything.'

58
00:04:54,063 --> 00:05:01,551
Busted. Proper paint system — primer,
base, clear — seals the alloy. Stops

59
00:05:01,901 --> 00:05:07,901
Especially here. Salt air, brake dust,
heat cycles. Bare alloy corrodes fast.

60
00:05:08,251 --> 00:05:14,035
And Desert Diamond bakes the finish. That
cross-links the clear coat. Real

61
00:05:14,384 --> 00:05:17,120
So it's protection *and* looks. Not
either-or.

62
00:05:17,470 --> 00:05:19,582
Myth busted. Next.

63
00:05:19,932 --> 00:05:22,044
That's our show. Thanks for listening.

64
00:05:22,394 --> 00:05:26,426
If your wheels need a refresh — or you
just want them to match the rest of the

65
00:05:26,776 --> 00:05:33,400
Desert Diamond. Al Quoz, 22nd Street. Or
Abu Dhabi. Book at car-care.center.

66
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:35,238
See you next episode.

67
00:05:35,588 --> 00:05:37,748
Drive safe. Keep it shiny.
